{"id":"74f141d193148576cdf2545090ba5dac21d3900a","axis":"silent","repo":"apache/beam","sha":"74f141d193148576cdf2545090ba5dac21d3900a","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".github/trigger_files/IO_Iceberg_Integration_Tests.json","lines":["@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@"," {","     \"comment\": \"Modify this file in a trivial way to cause this test suite to run.\",","-    \"modification\": 1","+    \"modification\": 2"," }"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"CHANGES.md","lines":["@@ -100,6 +100,7 @@"," * (Go) Added the standard `millis_instant` and `decimal` logical types for cross-language rows ([#39684](https://github.com/apache/beam/issues/39684))."," * [Beam SQL] Added `PRIMARY KEY (...) NOT ENFORCED` to `CREATE EXTERNAL TABLE`, and `ALTER TABLE ... ADD/DROP PRIMARY KEY` ([#40826](https://github.com/apache/beam/issues/40826))."," * [Beam SQL] Added a `WITH (...)` clause to set per-statement connector options in `FROM` and `INSERT INTO` ([#40848](https://github.com/apache/beam/issues/40848)).","+* [Beam SQL] Added `CHANGES(table [, start [, end]])` to read a table's changes in `FROM`, starting with Iceberg tables ([#40982](https://github.com/apache/beam/issues/40982))."," * (Python) `BatchElements` can group elements by key across workers (`key_fn`, `num_shards`), and RunInference model handlers can use it through `batch_key_fn` / `batch_key_num_shards`. `apache_beam.ml.inference.prefix_batching` adds a `PrefixBatchingConfig` and prompt/chat prefix extractors so LLM handlers can batch requests that share a prompt prefix and hit the server's prefix cache ([#40905](https://github.com/apache/beam/pull/40905))."," * (Go) Added pass-through registration for fixed and variable length string and bytes logical types ([#39684](https://github.com/apache/beam/issues/39684))."," "],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"sdks/java/extensions/sql/build.gradle","lines":["@@ -152,9 +152,10 @@ task copyFmppTemplatesFromSrc(type: Copy) {"," }"," "," // config.fmpp adds Beam's rules to Calcite's grammar, Parser.jj, only at fixed hooks. There is","-// no hook that allows us to add syntax right after a table name, which is needed to set options","-// using WITH ('key' = value, ...). To get around this, the copyFmppTemplatesFromCalciteCore task","-// edits its copy of Parser.jj to add that syntax.","+// no hook that allows us to add syntax right after a table name or a table function call, which is","+// needed to set options using WITH ('key' = value, ...) and to read changes using CHANGES(...). To","+// get around this, the copyFmppTemplatesFromCalciteCore task edits its copy of Parser.jj to add","+// that syntax."," //"," // Each entry below pairs a snippet of Calcite's grammar, the anchor, with Beam code. The task"," // inserts the code right after the anchor. Take the first entry. TableRef3, Calcite's rule for a","@@ -170,15 +171,20 @@ task copyFmppTemplatesFromSrc(type: Copy) {"," def calciteParserExtensions = [","   // Parses WITH on a table in FROM. This is the example above.","   '[ tableRef = Snapshot(tableRef) ]': 'tableRef = TableClauseOpt(tableRef, TableClause.Role.READ)',","+  // Parses WITH after a table function call in FROM, such as CHANGES(orders, 5). A CHANGES(...)","+  // call then gets folded into the name of the table it reads, like a table with WITH.","+  'tableRef = ImplicitTableFunctionCallArgs(tableName)': 'tableRef = ChangesCallOpt(tableRef)',","+  // Rejects TABLE(CHANGES(...)), so that FROM CHANGES(...) is the one way to read changes.","+  'tableRef = TableFunctionCall()': '{ TableClause.checkNotChanges(tableRef); }',","   // Parses WITH on the INSERT target, in Calcite's SqlInsert rule, before the optional column list.","   '[ LOOKAHEAD(5) tableRef = ExtendTable(tableRef) ]': 'tableRef = TableClauseOpt(tableRef, TableClause.Role.WRITE)',","-  // Beam gives a FROM table with WITH an alias: its own name. If the query gives it an alias too,","-  // keep only the query's. This runs at the end of TableRef3.","+  // Beam gives a FROM table with CHANGES(...) or WITH an alias: its own name. If the query gives it","+  // an alias too, keep only the query's. This runs at the end of TableRef3.","   '[ tableRef = Tablesample(tableRef) ]': '{ tableRef = TableClause.collapseImplicitAlias(tableRef); }',","   // SQL also uses WITH for common table expressions, as in WITH q AS (...) SELECT * FROM q. A","-  // reference to q can't take WITH options. They would become part of the name, and Calcite would","-  // then look for a catalog table instead of using q. addWith builds every such query, so check","-  // the references there.","+  // reference to q can't use CHANGES(...) or take WITH options. Either would become part of the","+  // name, and Calcite would then look for a catalog table instead of using q. addWith builds every","+  // such query, so check the references there.","   'JAVACODE SqlNode addWith(SqlNodeList withList, SqlNode e) {': 'TableClause.checkCteReferences(withList, e);',","   // OrderByLimitOpt attaches the ORDER BY of such a query after addWith has run, so check the","   // ORDER BY here too."],"additions":14,"deletions":8,"truncated":false},{"path":"sdks/java/extensions/sql/iceberg/build.gradle","lines":["@@ -42,8 +42,9 @@ dependencies {","   implementation library.java.vendored_guava_32_1_2_jre","   implementation library.java.vendored_calcite_1_40_0","   implementation library.java.jackson_databind","+  implementation library.java.joda_time"," ","-  testImplementation library.java.joda_time","+  testImplementation project(\":sdks:java:extensions:sql:jdbc\")","   testImplementation library.java.junit","   testImplementation library.java.google_api_services_bigquery","   testImplementation \"org.apache.iceberg:iceberg-api:1.9.2\""],"additions":2,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"sdks/java/extensions/sql/iceberg/src/main/java/org/apache/beam/sdk/extensions/sql/meta/provider/iceberg/IcebergChangesTable.java","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,233 @@","+/*","+ * Lic